<title>USA: Fed approves Toronto-Dominion takeover bid.</title>
<headline>Fed approves Toronto-Dominion takeover bid.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve approved an application by Toronto-Dominion Bank of Canada to acquire all the voting shares of Waterhouse Investor Services Inc. of New York and its subsidiary bank.</p>
<p>Toronto-Dominion Bank is the fifth largest bank in Canada with assets of $84.5 billion. It already underwrites and deals in debt and equity securities in the United States.</p>
<p>Waterhouse is the 34th largest bank in New York state with deposits of about $609 million. It also provides discount brokerage services to retail customers throughout the United States.</p>
</text>
